+### Adversarial and Contrastive Losses
+A variant that integrates pose-aware contrastive learning with adversarial training for 3D Gaussian splat generation [S4]. The discriminator includes a pose branch $d_p$ estimating a pose embedding $p_I$ from input images, while a pose encoder maps camera parameters $\theta$ to $p_\theta$ [S4]. The adversarial loss uses a softplus function with R1 regularization: $L_{adv} = \mathbb{E}_{z,\theta}[f(d(g(z,\theta)))] + \mathbb{E}_{I_r}[f(-d(I_r)) + \lambda||\nabla d(I_r)||^2]$ where $f(t) = -\log(1 + \exp(-t))$ [S4]. Contrastive pose loss $L_{pose}$ maximizes cosine similarity between $p_I$ and $p_\theta$ at temperature $\tau$ [S4]. Positional regularization uses $L_{center}$ to anchor coarsest-level Gaussians to the origin and $L_{knn}$ to minimize distances between $K$ nearest neighbors [S4]. The total objective is $L = L_{adv} + \lambda_{pose} L_{pose} + \lambda_{center} L_{center} + \lambda_{knn} L_{knn}$ [S4].
